{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa870cd0534b1d1fb899c72be85669782d6e44e36f36b5c13ea39966317e95db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler idempotency test","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311","binding_store_mod._now_iso","binding_lifecycle._now_iso","clear_absent","binding_lifecycle.py:45","binding_lifecycle.py:296","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence","binding_walk.py:254","outbound_differ.py:675"],"problem_keywords":["idempotency","oracle","clock patching","binding lifecycle","test coverage","integration test","module clock","timestamp stamping"],"propositions":["The idempotency oracle patches _now_iso only on binding_store, but RP-02 S2 T2 moved clear_absent and sibling operations into binding_lifecycle, which resolves its own module-level _now_iso, so the patch no longer reaches those operations.","The integration test's blast radius narrowed after the refactoring; it would no longer catch regressions where clear_absent stamps updated_at unconditionally on unchanged passes.","The idempotency test must patch _now_iso on both binding_store and binding_lifecycle modules to restore the oracle's original reach and coverage.","clear_absent is structurally unreachable on healthy in-window passes because both call sites (binding_walk:254 and outbound_differ:675) gate on out-of-window keys, so seeding an unconditional-stamp mutation cannot drive the integration test red."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":178729767971